<title>EGYPT: Telemisr half-yr profits up 226 pct.</title>
<headline>Telemisr half-yr profits up 226 pct.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Telemisr/Arab Radio Transistor and Electronics Supplies said on Wednesday it made net after-tax profits of 6.140 million pounds ($1.81 million) in the first six months of the financial year 1996/7, against 1.882 million in the same period of 1995/6. The years start July 1.</p>
<p>The company has two million shares and they closed on the Egyptian stock exchange at 40.16 pounds a share on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Here are the company's profit/loss acounts for the period (all figures in thousands of pounds):</p>
<p>				     July-Dec 1996    July-Dec 1995</p>
<p> Sales net of tax		   101,328	     62,305</p>
<p> Cost of production		  80,542	     50,855</p>
<p> Gross profit			  20,786	     11,450</p>
<p> Gross profit less expenses	 9,046		3,310</p>
<p> Exceptional revenue		     94		  402</p>
<p>Gross profit plus exceptional</p>
<p>     revenue			    9,140		3,712</p>
<p> Net pre-tax profit		   9,030		2,768</p>
<p> Tax					2,890		  886</p>
<p> Net attributable profit	    6,140		1,882</p>
<p>$1 = 3.395 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1 ($ = 3.39 Egyptian Pounds)</p>
